ELove the Sin: Sexual Regulation and the Limits of Religious Tolerance"“
In 1925, Diana Pollexfen was found innocent of killing her husband, but the accusation shadowed the rest of her life. Sixty years later, Diana's grandniece resolves to determine just who did kill George Pollexfen in that sunlit garden between the wars. First U.S. edition."§
¤Kallima Hamilton, Roger Kees, Kristen Berger, Rodney Nelson, Kyle Hemmings, Benjamin Saphiro, Raphael Cohen, Jnana Hodson, Adam Steiner, Nathan Hondros, Gary Back, Allison Grayhurst, Stephanie Guo, Doug Draime, Seymour Roth, Dan Hedges, Samuel McGrath, Joseph Kees, Michael Brownstein, Alain Marciano, Joschua von Beres, Giuseppi Martino Buonaiuto, Mark Murphey, Susan Dale, Laura Minning, Evan Iresmith, Lauren Frament, Chrissie Gittins, John Flynn, Lance Manion, Jeremiah Walton, James  Schwartz, Nostrovia! Poetry, Louis   Marvin, Paul Hostovsky"¯
¬Dianne Poppert has learned to trust that there is something greater in life-something that encourages unconditional love, illustrates the wonder of God's grace, and sustains the natural world. In her debut collection of poems, Poppert invites others to join her in witnessing the beauty within every day. Poppert reflects on a wide variety of themes that include the day she discovered where the dragonfly sleeps; the moments she watched magenta light introduce the evening and the sunset splash mysterious artistry across the sky; and the indescribable joy she embraced as her granddaughters entered the world. Through graceful wordplay and vivid imagery, Poppert teaches all of us to look for the good, find the courage to just be, and practice gratitude for the simple gifts that life often brings. Shadows of a Pretty River offers a poignant glimpse into one woman's life as she leads others down a lyrical path into her heart and soul."¶
